@april_2023
# prose-audit: Grade A — The two-party alliance is grounded in its leaders and organisations, while Lewica's responses change with its live democratic-opposition or PiS-aligned role.
title: Two parties choose a third road
tags: poland_event, poland_event_calendar
priority: 32
order: 90
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2023 and month = 4 and third_way_2023_done = 0
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-holownia.webp
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
const finiteThirdWay = function(value, fallback) {
    return Number.isFinite(Number(value)) ? Number(value) : fallback;
};
const mayListStrategy = String(Q.may22_list_strategy || "");
Q.third_way_pis_aligned_left =
    (
        Q.left_in_government && Q.government_party == "pis"
    ) || mayListStrategy.includes("PiS host-list") ? 1 : 0;
const thirdWaySocialFit = (
    finiteThirdWay(Q.psl_accept_social, 38) +
    finiteThirdWay(Q.p2050_accept_social, 46)
) / 2;
const thirdWayOpenness = (
    finiteThirdWay(Q.psl_coalition_openness, 35) +
    finiteThirdWay(Q.p2050_coalition_openness, 47)
) / 2;
Q.third_way_nonaggression_open =
    thirdWaySocialFit >= 36 && thirdWayOpenness >= 38 ? 1 : 0;
Q.third_way_p2050_channel_open =
    finiteThirdWay(Q.p2050_coalition_openness, 47) >= 48 ? 1 : 0;
Q.third_way_relation_payoff = Math.max(
    1,
    Math.min(
        6,
        Math.round((thirdWaySocialFit + thirdWayOpenness - 50) / 12)
    )
);
Q.third_way_2023_done = 1;
Q.third_way_active = 1;
Q.third_way_split = 0;
Q.third_way_cohesion = Number.isFinite(Number(Q.third_way_cohesion))
    ? Number(Q.third_way_cohesion)
    : 58;
Q.rival_relation_psl_p2050 = Math.max(
    68,
    Number(Q.rival_relation_psl_p2050) || 58
);
Q.news_headline = "PSL and Poland 2050 create Third Way";
!}

= April 2023 — Two parties, one threshold

On 27 April, <span class="party-p2050"><b>Szymon Hołownia</b></span> and <span class="party-psl"><b>Władysław Kosiniak-Kamysz</b></span> announce that
Poland 2050 and PSL will contest the election together. This is an electoral
coalition, not a merger. Hołownia remains the reformist national face; Kosiniak-
Kamysz still commands a party built through county offices, mayors and agrarian
networks.

Each principal supplies what the other lacks. Poland 2050 brings a new brand,
volunteers and voters who want administrative competence. PSL brings durable
local structures and candidates who have survived elections before. Both
leaders reject Tusk's demand for one opposition list, but their common
committee must clear the higher coalition threshold.

[? if not third_way_pis_aligned_left: For us, Third Way is a necessary partner
against PiS, a rival for social and rural voters, and a threshold risk that can
decide whether the democratic opposition wins a majority.?]
[? if third_way_pis_aligned_left: We no longer meet Third Way from the same
opposition camp. Our PiS alignment makes Hołownia and Kosiniak-Kamysz electoral
adversaries of the governing bloc; repeating Tusk's one-list demand would make
no political sense.?]

- @apr23_nonaggression
- @apr23_counties
- @apr23_one_list
- @apr23_peel
- @apr23_governing_attack

