@mar23_resolution
# prose-audit: Grade B — The resolution vote reads back March's stance in prose and in what remains choosable, and the survivor-testimony route is locked to having funded the network; the deputies who abstained are not individually named.
title: The resolution is put to a vote
subtitle: The Sejm decides whether to legislate a reputation
face-image: img/poland/events/john-paul-ii-monument.webp
new-page: true

= April 2023 — A chamber votes on a memory

The resolution reaches the floor: the Sejm is asked to declare its defence of
the good name of John Paul II against what the text calls a shameful media
campaign inspired by foreign interests. It has no legal effect whatsoever. It
will be read for a decade as a roll call of who could and could not be made to
sign a statement about a dead pope six months before an election.

PSL will vote for it. KO will find a formula. Konfederacja will vote for it
loudly. Our own caucus contains practising Catholics from counties where this
vote is the only thing anybody will remember about the Left this year.

[? if church_2023_stance = "Historical scrutiny": In March we refused a
state-enforced sacred memory, so nobody expects us to sign now and the only
question is what we say instead.?]
[? if church_2023_stance = "Survivors first": In March we paid for lawyers and
an archive team rather than a studio quarrel, and the people who used that
service are the reason this vote is not abstract to us.?]
[? if church_2023_stance = "Faith without impunity": In March we separated
faith from institutional impunity, which is the hardest position to hold in a
roll call with two columns.?]
[? if church_2023_stance = "Stayed out": In March we changed the subject.
There is no changing it today; the clerk will read our names out one at a
time.?]

- @mar23_res_against
- @mar23_res_testimony
- @mar23_res_free_vote

@mar23_res_against
title: Vote against as a caucus and publish the constitutional reason
subtitle: Consistent and disciplined; in a dozen rural constituencies it is the vote our candidates will spend 2023 answering for.
on-arrival: {!
