Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica releases its deputies and splits on the John Paul II resolution";
!}

The whip is lifted. Eleven of our deputies vote for the resolution, the rest
against, and two are recorded as absent in a way that fools nobody.

The eastern constituencies are held. Every equality organisation that spent
2020 in the street with us reads the division list, and a party that asked them
to believe it had a position discovers that a free vote is also a position, and
a legible one.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue

@apr23_grain
# prose-audit: Grade B — The border closure, the minister's resignation and the collision between farmers and Ukraine policy are staged with a locked transition route; the Ukrainian hauliers are named as a category.
title: The grain at the border
subtitle: A minister resigns and the frontier closes to Ukrainian grain
face-image: img/poland/events/farmers-protest-2024.webp
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.apr23_grain_done = 1;
Q.rural_support = (Number(Q.rural_support) || 0) - 2;
Q.ukraine_solidarity = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.ukraine_solidarity) || 50) - 8
);
Q.eu_relations = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.eu_relations) || 45) - 4
);
Q.public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support += -9;
Q.public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_salience += 10;
Q.public_mood_pending_border_security_support += 5;
Q.news_headline =
    "The agriculture minister resigns and Poland closes the border to Ukrainian grain";
!}

= April 2023 — Solidarity meets a silo

The corridors opened to move Ukrainian grain to world markets did not move it
to world markets. A great deal of it stopped in Poland, where it was cheaper
than the domestic crop, and by spring Polish farmers are sitting on last
year's harvest with nowhere to sell it. Tractors are on the roads in the east.

**Henryk Kowalczyk**, the agriculture minister, resigns on 5 April. Ten days
later the government unilaterally bans imports of Ukrainian grain and several
other products — a measure that is almost certainly outside Poland's
competence, since trade policy belongs to the Union, and which the Commission
says so about immediately.

The politics are brutally simple. The government is being outflanked on its own
right by farmers' organisations, an election is six months away, and the
country that has spent a year being the most reliably pro-Ukrainian state in
Europe has just closed its border to Ukrainian goods.

[? if rural_support < 30: Our standing in farming counties is poor enough that
nobody there is waiting to hear what the Left thinks about this.?]
[? if animal_bill_compensation = 1: We attached compensation and retraining to
the fur-farm ban in 2020, which is the one time this party arrived in a farming
county with money rather than a principle.?]
[? if ukraine_solidarity >= 60: Public solidarity with Ukraine is still high,
which makes the closure look opportunistic and makes opposing it survivable.?]

- @grain23_transit
- @grain23_farmers
- @grain23_ban

@grain23_transit
title: Demand a European transit and storage solution instead of a border
subtitle: The correct answer and the one that requires somebody else to act; farmers will hear a refusal.
on-arrival: {!
Q.grain_2023_stance = "European transit solution";
Q.eu_relations = (Number(Q.eu_relations) || 41) + 6;
Q.ukraine_solidarity =
    (Number(Q.ukraine_solidarity) || 42) + 5;
Q.foreign_policy_capacity =
    (Number(Q.foreign_policy_capacity) || 0) + 3;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 2;
Q.rural_support = (Number(Q.rural_support) || 0) - 3;
Q.konf_poll_momentum =
    (Number(Q.konf_poll_momentum) || 0) + 0.15;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left asks Brussels for transit capacity instead of a closed frontier";
!}

Rail capacity, port slots, sealed transit and Union money to pay for the
storage — the answer that moves the grain to the countries that need it instead
of leaving it in Polish silos. It is what the corridors were supposed to be.

It is also a promise about Brussels made to a man with a full barn in April.
Konfederacja is already in those counties saying that the Left cares more about
Ukrainian exporters than Polish farmers, and this month we hand them the
quotation.

- @apr23_missile: Turn to the woods near Bydgoszcz

@grain23_farmers
title: Support the farmers with a purchase guarantee and a transition fund
subtitle: Requires having paid for an agricultural transition before. Buys the right to oppose the border closure.
choose-if: animal_bill_compensation = 1 or just_transition_pledge = 1
