Q.eu_relations = (Number(Q.eu_relations) || 41) + 2;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 3;
Q.psl_relation = (Number(Q.psl_relation) || 0) + 5;
Q.household_policy_pressure =
    (Number(Q.household_policy_pressure) || 0) + 3;
Q.konf_poll_momentum =
    (Number(Q.konf_poll_momentum) || 0) - 0.1;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left answers the border closure with a purchase guarantee for farmers";
!}

An intervention purchase at a floor price, storage paid for, and a transition
fund for the smallest holdings — the same structure we used when we closed the
fur farms, which is why farming organisations take the meeting rather than the
photograph.

It costs money and it means we can say the sentence that matters: the border
does not have to close, because the problem is a price and a silo rather than a
Ukrainian. In two eastern voivodeships that argument is heard for the first
time from somebody other than the right.

- @apr23_missile: Turn to the woods near Bydgoszcz

@grain23_ban
title: Back the closure and let the Commission argue with Warsaw
subtitle: The popular answer in the counties that matter; it endorses a unilateral breach of Union trade competence six months before an election.
