Q.missile_2023_stance = "Reporting standard";
Q.defence_readiness = (Number(Q.defence_readiness) || 40) + 7;
Q.civil_military_trust =
    (Number(Q.civil_military_trust) || 38) + 10;
Q.security_incident_pressure = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.security_incident_pressure) || 0) - 6
);
Q.institutional_trust = (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) + 5;
Q.administrative_reform_pressure =
    (Number(Q.administrative_reform_pressure) || 0) + 4;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 3;
Q.news_headline =
    "One reporting chain is demanded from radar contact to the minister's desk";
!}

The question is written so that it cannot be answered with a briefing: at what
point does an unidentified contact become a notification, to whom, in what time
and with what record. Then the second question — who may call off a search, and
who is told when they do.

Officers answer this one, quietly and in detail, because it is the question
they have been asking internally for a year. The standard that eventually
exists is written from those answers, and it is the reason later incidents
produce a document instead of three ministries contradicting each other.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue

@missile23_blame
title: Make the defence minister answer for four months of silence
subtitle: The obvious attack in an election year; the services conclude that saying less is safer.
on-arrival: {!
Q.missile_2023_stance = "Ministerial blame";
Q.left_poll_momentum =
    (Number(Q.left_poll_momentum) || 0) + 0.15;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 2;
Q.pis_relation = (Number(Q.pis_relation) || 0) - 8;
Q.civil_military_trust = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.civil_military_trust) || 38) - 6
);
Q.defence_readiness = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.defence_readiness) || 40) - 2
);
Q.media_capacity = (Number(Q.media_capacity) || 0) + 3;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left makes the missile a question about the defence minister";
!}

Seven years of the largest defence budget in Polish history and a cruise
missile sat in a wood for four months. The line is fair, it is devastating, and
it is repeated in every studio until October.

Inside the services the lesson taken is the wrong one and the obvious one: an
incident reported upwards becomes an opposition clip, so the next one is
reported later, higher and in vaguer language. The command culture we complain
about in 2026 is partly built this spring.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue

@missile23_civil
title: Ask what the people living there were supposed to have been told
subtitle: Moves the argument from the ministry to the woodland and the town; smaller, slower and it reaches people the defence argument never does.
on-arrival: {!
Q.missile_2023_stance = "Civil protection";
Q.defence_readiness = (Number(Q.defence_readiness) || 40) + 3;
Q.local_network = (Number(Q.local_network) || 0) + 3;
Q.rural_support = (Number(Q.rural_support) || 0) + 3;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 4;
Q.institutional_trust = (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) + 3;
Q.administrative_reform_pressure =
    (Number(Q.administrative_reform_pressure) || 0) + 3;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left asks what the villages near the crash site were ever told";
!}

We go to the commune. Nobody there was notified, nobody was asked to avoid the
area, and the man who found it did what anybody would do, which was photograph
it and telephone somebody.

Our question is what a resident is entitled to be told and by whom. It is
smaller than the ministerial argument and it produces the first draft of a
notification duty that matters enormously later, when things start falling out
of the sky more often.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue
